 ## Background
-*   **Origin:** The method was introduced by T. L. Kay and J. T. Kajiya in their 1986 paper "Ray tracing complex scenes" presented at SIGGRAPH [S2, unofficial][S3].
-*   **Development:** The algorithm has become the standard for AABB intersection in ray tracing. It is widely used in modern ray tracing kernels such as Embree and in astronomical simulation tools like raytheia [S2, unofficial][S3].
-*   **Usage:** It is used for primary ray-scene intersection testing, shadow ray occlusion testing, frustum culling, and spatial traversal of octree and grid acceleration structures [S4].
